---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Layout title="Docs - Rafters">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">Getting Started</h1>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Install</h2>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Rafters is registry-delivered. No packages to install. The CLI fetches source files
        directly into your project.
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-4 mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>pnpx rafters init</code></pre>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        This creates a <code class="bg-neutral-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">.rafters/</code> directory with your design tokens
        and configuration. Tokens are generated from mathematical rules, not hand-picked values.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Add components</h2>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-4 mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>pnpx rafters add button dialog form</code></pre>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Components land in your project as source files you own. Each one carries embedded
        intelligence metadata: cognitive load scores, do/never rules, accessibility requirements,
        and dependency declarations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Start the MCP server</h2>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-4 mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>pnpx rafters mcp</code></pre>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        This gives your AI agent access to five tools: vocabulary lookup, pattern guidance,
        component intelligence, token semantics, and cognitive budget review. Your agent stops
        guessing and starts reasoning about design.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Open Studio</h2>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-100 rounded-lg p-4 mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>pnpx rafters studio</code></pre>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
        The visual editor for your design system rules. Configure spacing progressions, type scales,
        color relationships, and motion philosophy. Changes regenerate tokens automatically.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
